config INPUT_KBD_MATRIX_SHARED_BUS
	bool "GPIO keyboard matrix sharing pins with another device"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_GPIO_KBD_MATRIX_SHARED_BUS_ENABLED
	select INPUT_KBD_MATRIX
	help
	  Keyboard matrix input driver for boards where the sensed (row) GPIOs
	  are time-shared with another peripheral (e.g. a parallel-bus LCD)
	  rather than owned exclusively.

	  Unlike CONFIG_INPUT_GPIO_KBD_MATRIX, this driver has no interrupt or
	  internal polling thread of its own — it never touches the shared
	  pins except during a scan. The application must call
	  kbd_matrix_shared_bus_scan() explicitly, from the same thread that
	  drives the other peripheral sharing the pins, whenever it wants a
	  scan to happen (e.g. once per display refresh). See
	  include/drivers/input/kbd_matrix_shared_bus.h.
